1
00:00:00,777 --> 00:00:09,157
I found myself lost and alone on this journey

2
00:00:09,157 --> 00:00:17,497
Though my heart wandered far and wide, I could move not an inch

3
00:00:17,497 --> 00:00:22,587
But now I can depart for any distant land

4
00:00:22,587 --> 00:00:25,717
But now I can depart for any distant land

5
00:00:25,717 --> 00:00:28,757
Now that we've met on this road

6
00:00:28,757 --> 00:00:34,557
Now that we've met on this road

7
00:00:35,057 --> 00:00:42,397
Even the unfamiliar songs of travelers

8
00:00:42,397 --> 00:00:53,157
Can spark nostalgia in me when I'm with you

9
00:00:53,157 --> 00:00:57,037
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

10
00:00:57,037 --> 00:01:01,417
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

11
00:01:01,417 --> 00:01:09,847
Then let's go search for it beyond the wind

12
00:01:09,847 --> 00:01:13,807
Through chilling dawns,

13
00:01:13,807 --> 00:01:18,227
Through arid noons,

14
00:01:18,227 --> 00:01:22,187
Through shivering nights,

15
00:01:22,187 --> 00:01:28,197
Let's go see what lies at the end

16
00:01:39,827 --> 00:01:40,787
What's the matter?

17
00:01:41,287 --> 00:01:43,417
There are tremors in the air.

18
00:01:46,297 --> 00:01:48,377
We're near the market.

19
00:01:49,337 --> 00:01:50,677
Isn't that the cause?

20
00:01:51,347 --> 00:01:52,637
No, I can feel it.

21
00:01:53,427 --> 00:01:54,557
Water?

22
00:01:58,437 --> 00:02:01,097
The sound of splashing water.

23
00:02:03,767 --> 00:02:04,817
Where?

24
00:02:06,187 --> 00:02:07,147
Ahead of us.

25
00:02:07,147 --> 00:02:08,897
This won't do. We have to turn back!

26
00:02:09,317 --> 00:02:11,177
Is this the only path?

27
00:02:12,067 --> 00:02:14,987
There weren't any forks in the direction we were going.

28
00:02:14,987 --> 00:02:18,957
Even I lack the confidence to find my way around here.

29
00:02:22,377 --> 00:02:22,997
What's wrong?

30
00:02:22,997 --> 00:02:24,997
They'll catch us even if we run.

31
00:02:24,997 --> 00:02:26,997
They've set dogs after us.

32
00:02:27,007 --> 00:02:27,967
What?

33
00:02:28,917 --> 00:02:30,677
So foolish-sounding, that baying.

34
00:02:31,087 --> 00:02:33,507
You should cover your ears.

35
00:02:51,317 --> 00:02:52,777
What the hell was that?

36
00:03:03,327 --> 00:03:05,337
I want some apples...

37
00:03:07,587 --> 00:03:09,747
I'll buy you as many as you'd like later.

38
00:03:09,747 --> 00:03:14,757
Wolf and a Silent Farewell

39
00:03:14,757 --> 00:03:16,927
How on earth did they find us?

40
00:03:16,927 --> 00:03:20,387
They probably ran into us by chance while they were looking underground.

41
00:03:20,387 --> 00:03:22,517
If they knew exactly where we were, they would have cornered us by now.

42
00:03:26,977 --> 00:03:29,387
Milone Trading has betrayed you!

43
00:03:30,107 --> 00:03:32,077
There's no point in running!

44
00:03:32,567 --> 00:03:34,907
Sounds like we've been sold out.

45
00:03:40,447 --> 00:03:42,367
We must have come at a high price.

46
00:03:43,207 --> 00:03:46,747
After all, they can run Milone's branch office into the ground if they have you.

47
00:03:46,747 --> 00:03:50,207
I see. That would call for a high price indeed.

48
00:03:50,207 --> 00:03:53,547
Sounds like a garden variety bluff to me.

49
00:03:54,177 --> 00:03:56,007
Once we turn this corner...

50
00:04:00,677 --> 00:04:01,727
I found them!

51
00:04:02,727 --> 00:04:03,887
There they are!

52
00:04:03,887 --> 00:04:05,517
Don't let them get away!

53
00:04:06,107 --> 00:04:07,227
Do you know which—

54
00:04:07,227 --> 00:04:09,227
It's this way. We're fine!

55
00:04:16,277 --> 00:04:17,447
Turn left here!

56
00:04:18,487 --> 00:04:19,277
No!

57
00:04:28,337 --> 00:04:30,957
Sorry, but we're in a hurry.

58
00:04:38,007 --> 00:04:39,137
Lawrence!

59
00:04:40,387 --> 00:04:42,877
Lord Almighty, please forgive my sins.

60
00:04:50,767 --> 00:04:54,337
Even if God forgives you, it seems that you angered Lady Luck somewhere along the way.

61
00:05:03,657 --> 00:05:04,787
Damn it.

62
00:05:07,077 --> 00:05:08,627
He got me.

63
00:05:13,007 --> 00:05:14,087
Lawrence!

64
00:05:18,587 --> 00:05:19,887
What a relief.

65
00:05:20,427 --> 00:05:22,677
You weren't moving when I called to you.

66
00:05:27,477 --> 00:05:28,397
I'm fine.

67
00:05:29,227 --> 00:05:30,807
I was just a little tired.

68
00:05:34,567 --> 00:05:36,237
Pull it together.

69
00:05:36,237 --> 00:05:37,737
We're almost there.

70
00:05:37,737 --> 00:05:38,777
Where?

71
00:05:39,657 --> 00:05:41,237
Weren't you listening to me?

72
00:05:42,447 --> 00:05:44,237
I can smell the warmth of the sun ahead.

73
00:05:44,237 --> 00:05:46,907
Didn't I tell you there's a way to the surface nearby?

74
00:05:52,457 --> 00:05:54,877
Yeah, that's right.

75
00:05:56,587 --> 00:05:57,417
What's this?

76
00:05:57,797 --> 00:06:00,337
You didn't even notice <i>that</i>?

77
00:06:03,307 --> 00:06:05,177
No, of course I noticed. I'm fine.

78
00:06:08,307 --> 00:06:09,347
We're almost there.

79
00:06:10,557 --> 00:06:13,517
We'll be at the exit once we turn right at the end of the path.

80
00:06:14,267 --> 00:06:14,817
Look!

81
00:06:21,027 --> 00:06:22,657
It can't be...

82
00:06:22,657 --> 00:06:23,947
An abandoned well, huh?

83
00:06:26,077 --> 00:06:30,497
I'm sorry. I didn't think it'd end up like this.

84
00:06:30,497 --> 00:06:31,577
There they are!

85
00:06:33,497 --> 00:06:34,797
We found them!

86
00:06:36,297 --> 00:06:37,337
Stay back.

87
00:06:37,337 --> 00:06:38,547
No...

88
00:06:39,547 --> 00:06:41,217
You can't—you're barely standing!

89
00:06:42,007 --> 00:06:43,127
Don't you worry.

90
00:06:44,047 --> 00:06:45,427
I'll be just fine.

91
00:06:45,887 --> 00:06:49,347
That's a lie! I don't need my ears to know that's a lie!

92
00:06:56,277 --> 00:07:00,257
I wondered, given the description we got.

93
00:07:00,257 --> 00:07:02,447
But who would have thought it'd really be you,

94
00:07:03,617 --> 00:07:04,587
Lawrence.

95
00:07:07,407 --> 00:07:10,867
The man behind Medio Trading is Count Ehrendott.

96
00:07:11,457 --> 00:07:17,797
A large wheat-producing land is capable of designating a silver currency of their choice for all their transactions.

97
00:07:17,797 --> 00:07:22,797
The elimination of wheat tariffs would be a blessing not only for Medio Trading and the Count,

98
00:07:22,797 --> 00:07:26,137
but for those in the village as well.

99
00:07:26,807 --> 00:07:29,767
You personally know the merchants who buy wheat from the village.

100
00:07:30,387 --> 00:07:32,847
The village chief has entrusted everything to you as well.

101
00:07:32,847 --> 00:07:37,647
Wheat sales reach their peak right after the harvest, too.

102
00:07:40,817 --> 00:07:43,987
Well, let's catch up later.

103
00:07:43,987 --> 00:07:45,277
We don't have much time.

104
00:07:45,277 --> 00:07:46,527
Don't be so cold.

105
00:07:47,027 --> 00:07:50,027
We hardly got to see each other when I last visited.

106
00:07:50,027 --> 00:07:53,287
Ah, but you met someone else, didn't you?

107
00:07:55,617 --> 00:07:57,917
Hand her over to us.

108
00:07:57,917 --> 00:08:03,127
We'll present her to the Church and put the old ways to rest forever.

109
00:08:04,007 --> 00:08:08,177
If we do that, we'll be able to destroy Milone Trading.

110
00:08:08,177 --> 00:08:14,347
When the tariffs are lifted, the profit from our wheat will skyrocket,

111
00:08:14,347 --> 00:08:17,517
and those we sell it to will be rich indeed.

112
00:08:18,147 --> 00:08:25,437
Lawrence, our village still remembers that you bought
wheat from us when we were suffering from heavy taxation.

113
00:08:26,447 --> 00:08:30,277
It would be no trouble to give you purchasing priority now.

114
00:08:31,197 --> 00:08:32,197
Lawrence...

115
00:08:33,367 --> 00:08:37,167
Let's finalize this deal and open a store in this town together.

116
00:08:37,167 --> 00:08:40,837
As a merchant, surely you can figure gain and loss.

117
00:08:43,297 --> 00:08:44,127
You're right.

118
00:08:45,717 --> 00:08:48,127
I've always wanted to realize that dream.

119
00:08:54,807 --> 00:08:55,887
Lawrence!

120
00:08:55,887 --> 00:09:00,977
However, an honest merchant abides by his contracts.

121
00:09:03,647 --> 00:09:05,397
Fate works in strange ways.

122
00:09:05,397 --> 00:09:08,777
A peculiar wolf I've picked up wants to return to the north.

123
00:09:09,867 --> 00:09:13,577
I have a contract to accompany her there.

124
00:09:13,577 --> 00:09:16,997
It goes against my principles to willingly breach a contract.

125
00:09:16,997 --> 00:09:18,127
You...

126
00:09:22,587 --> 00:09:24,627
I'm sorry our friendship was a short one.

127
00:09:25,547 --> 00:09:27,757
A merchant is always saying goodbye.

128
00:09:35,727 --> 00:09:37,387
You can kill the man.

129
00:09:37,897 --> 00:09:40,397
Bring <i>her</i> in alive.

130
00:09:44,437 --> 00:09:45,897
Let's see what you've got.

131
00:09:51,407 --> 00:09:52,867
Holo!

132
00:09:53,737 --> 00:09:54,827
My dagger!

133
00:09:56,787 --> 00:09:58,247
Enough!

134
00:09:58,247 --> 00:10:00,497
This might hurt a little...

135
00:10:02,917 --> 00:10:04,417
Please bear with it.

136
00:10:15,717 --> 00:10:17,347
She's sucking his blood!

137
00:10:29,607 --> 00:10:33,657
Don't be afraid! She's only a possessed girl.

138
00:10:39,867 --> 00:10:40,787
Don't...

139
00:10:43,917 --> 00:10:45,377
Don't look at me.

140
00:12:36,987 --> 00:12:40,117
You gods are always like that...

141
00:12:41,077 --> 00:12:42,117
Always...

142
00:12:43,037 --> 00:12:45,497
Always making life unfair...

143
00:12:58,547 --> 00:12:59,507
Holo, don't!

144
00:13:37,927 --> 00:13:38,887
Wait!

145
00:13:41,307 --> 00:13:41,877
Holo!

146
00:13:48,057 --> 00:13:48,647
H...

147
00:13:50,727 --> 00:13:54,227
How much do you think those clothes you ruined cost me?

148
00:13:54,817 --> 00:13:57,987
I don't care if you're a god or not! You're going to pay for it in full!

149
00:13:58,737 --> 00:14:03,157
The fifty coins left over from what you earned aren't even a fraction of what you owe!

150
00:14:03,907 --> 00:14:07,327
How many years do you think it took me to save that kind of money?

151
00:14:09,117 --> 00:14:10,327
I'm going to follow you.

152
00:14:11,707 --> 00:14:13,747
I'll follow you to the northlands if I have to!

153
00:14:27,347 --> 00:14:28,807
Holo!

154
00:14:55,497 --> 00:14:57,377
You're awake, are you?

155
00:15:00,427 --> 00:15:02,677
How's your wound doing?

156
00:15:02,677 --> 00:15:05,177
It feels better, thank you.

157
00:15:06,767 --> 00:15:11,597
I must apologize for putting you through such danger through our ineptitude.

158
00:15:11,597 --> 00:15:15,857
Don't. My companion was the cause of this, after all.

159
00:15:18,687 --> 00:15:21,767
It was fortunate that the melee happened underground.

160
00:15:22,567 --> 00:15:28,027
If someone else saw her in that form, our headquarters and branch stores would be ablaze by now.

161
00:15:28,787 --> 00:15:30,327
You saw her true form?

162
00:15:30,327 --> 00:15:32,997
Yes. I received a report from an agent

163
00:15:33,577 --> 00:15:40,877
who said that a gigantic wolf would not hand you over until I came personally.

164
00:15:43,297 --> 00:15:45,137
What happened to Holo?

165
00:15:45,547 --> 00:15:49,637
She left without saying a word after we brought you here.

166
00:15:55,017 --> 00:15:56,897
I see.

167
00:16:13,327 --> 00:16:15,417
How did the negotiations go?

168
00:16:16,207 --> 00:16:20,507
We were able to obtain the rights that I expected Medio Trading would want most.

169
00:16:21,337 --> 00:16:23,087
That's wonderful.

170
00:16:23,087 --> 00:16:26,707
We were able to collect 307,112 silver coins.

171
00:16:27,047 --> 00:16:30,927
The king plans to reissue a severely depreciated version of the silver coins,

172
00:16:30,927 --> 00:16:36,187
and we are to be paid with the cash value of 350,000 pieces at the time of delivery.

173
00:16:36,187 --> 00:16:38,357
Three hundred and fifty thousand!

174
00:16:38,357 --> 00:16:43,607
Our contract was to pay you five percent of our profit.

175
00:16:43,607 --> 00:16:45,357
Do you have any objections?

176
00:16:46,987 --> 00:16:49,077
No, that's correct.

177
00:16:49,077 --> 00:16:50,697
Please confirm it for yourself.

178
00:16:54,327 --> 00:16:55,327
This is...

179
00:16:55,327 --> 00:16:59,917
One hundred and twenty silver coins. That is five percent of our profit.

180
00:17:01,417 --> 00:17:04,837
It only amounted... to this?

181
00:17:04,837 --> 00:17:10,057
Transportation costs for the coins
we collected, taxes levied on those very coins,

182
00:17:10,057 --> 00:17:13,337
and the processing fee for the contract were all taken into consideration.

183
00:17:14,767 --> 00:17:18,517
They imposed a rather excessive processing fee.

184
00:17:19,307 --> 00:17:21,227
The King's advisors probably put him up to it.

185
00:17:22,147 --> 00:17:27,487
They had to give up those privileges, but they minimized their losses on the currency exchange.

186
00:17:27,987 --> 00:17:30,737
It was beyond what we could foresee.

187
00:17:30,737 --> 00:17:33,157
It's just unfortunate.

188
00:17:34,957 --> 00:17:38,667
When it comes to business, expect the unexpected.

189
00:17:38,667 --> 00:17:39,877
However...

190
00:17:40,347 --> 00:17:45,757
Unexpected situations can work out happily as well.

191
00:17:50,547 --> 00:17:51,757
This is...

192
00:17:51,757 --> 00:17:55,767
Medio Trading was desperate for those special privileges.

193
00:17:55,767 --> 00:18:00,647
And they were collecting silver coins that were guaranteed to depreciate.

194
00:18:00,647 --> 00:18:03,817
Keeping them would be little different from holding a debt.

195
00:18:03,817 --> 00:18:07,897
They probably wanted to turn any kind of profit at this point in time.

196
00:18:08,657 --> 00:18:11,907
We didn't have to think twice about their offer.

197
00:18:11,907 --> 00:18:13,407
One thousand for me, though?

198
00:18:13,407 --> 00:18:15,147
Really, it's a trifle.

199
00:18:15,497 --> 00:18:17,577
Will silver coins be fine?

200
00:18:17,577 --> 00:18:20,997
If you'd prefer payment in commodities, we can have that arranged.

201
00:18:22,207 --> 00:18:23,167
Pepper.

202
00:18:24,627 --> 00:18:26,377
Do you have pepper?

203
00:18:26,377 --> 00:18:32,507
It's light, compact, and as winter falls, its price will rise as meat becomes more popular.

204
00:18:34,177 --> 00:18:35,517
Is something wrong?

205
00:18:35,517 --> 00:18:40,227
Excuse me. It just reminded me
of a particular play I recently read.

206
00:18:40,687 --> 00:18:41,477
Play?

207
00:18:41,477 --> 00:18:42,437
Indeed.

208
00:18:43,187 --> 00:18:47,947
A religious play created by the Church to advocate restraint among traders.

209
00:18:47,947 --> 00:18:52,767
Once upon a time, the devil appeared in front of a wealthy merchant.

210
00:18:52,767 --> 00:18:57,707
"Bring forth the tastiest human around or I shall devour you!"

211
00:18:57,707 --> 00:18:59,997
The merchant feared for his life.

212
00:18:59,997 --> 00:19:04,487
He offered a young maid and a fat serf, but the devil shook his head.

213
00:19:04,997 --> 00:19:07,937
After searching across the town for a luscious human being,

214
00:19:07,937 --> 00:19:12,257
he finally came across a boy who smelled of honey and milk.

215
00:19:12,257 --> 00:19:17,427
But when the merchant offered the boy to the devil, the boy said,

216
00:19:17,427 --> 00:19:20,977
"The tastiest human is right in front of you."

217
00:19:20,977 --> 00:19:24,977
What the devil saw was a man who ate spices daily,

218
00:19:24,977 --> 00:19:28,487
and whose fattened soul was perfectly seasoned.

219
00:19:32,197 --> 00:19:37,617
I was just imagining a fattened Mr. Lawrence
being devoured by the devil.

220
00:19:38,297 --> 00:19:41,537
I wouldn't mind having a body seasoned with spices.

221
00:19:41,537 --> 00:19:43,077
I'm looking forward to it.

222
00:19:44,207 --> 00:19:50,257
I'd like to have many fruitful dealings in the future, Mr. Lawrence.

223
00:19:51,087 --> 00:19:52,797
Thank you very much.

224
00:19:52,797 --> 00:19:55,007
I must return to my work.

225
00:20:01,727 --> 00:20:05,557
Mr. Lawrence, an invoice addressed to you has just arrived.

226
00:20:10,107 --> 00:20:11,727
I don't recall buying any of this.

227
00:20:24,327 --> 00:20:25,667
Which way is the loading dock?

228
00:20:25,667 --> 00:20:29,087
Go straight ahead, make a right, and...

229
00:20:29,087 --> 00:20:29,877
Thanks!

230
00:20:32,377 --> 00:20:33,377
Out of the way!

231
00:20:34,047 --> 00:20:34,927
Sorry!

232
00:20:36,047 --> 00:20:43,977
A robe, a silk sash, traveling shoes, a tortoiseshell comb,

233
00:20:49,147 --> 00:20:50,227
and last but not least,

234
00:20:55,317 --> 00:20:56,657
tons of apples.

235
00:20:57,237 --> 00:21:00,907
That'll be a total of a hundred and forty silver coins.

236
00:21:00,907 --> 00:21:02,117
Holo!

237
00:21:03,577 --> 00:21:05,117
Sorry, let me through.

238
00:21:15,377 --> 00:21:18,587
I wouldn't want you to come all the way to the northern woods just to collect on a debt.

239
00:21:22,927 --> 00:21:24,097
Geez.

240
00:21:46,497 --> 00:21:49,167
I'll return home only after I've repaid you.

241
00:21:52,627 --> 00:21:53,797
That goes without saying.

242
00:21:59,757 --> 00:22:02,717
Some spice and a wolf, huh?

243
00:23:40,987 --> 00:23:44,997
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and the Tail of Happiness."</i>

244
00:23:45,997 --> 00:23:49,997
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and the Tail of Happiness."</i>

